[2.095447, "o", "s written `path:Lstart-Lend`, relative to the Lear repository root, at commit `60cf9abf8408`. `python -m ragformation lear docs verify --source <checkout>` re-checks every reference against that commit. [1] They are the knowledge base of the `python -m ragformation lear` assistant, so every factual statement points at the code that supports it. - [implemented] Lear is packaged as the Python distribution `prash-v2` version 0.2.0, requires Python 3.10 or newer, and installs one console script, `prash`, mapped to `prash.cli:main`. [3] Subcommands (14): `run`, `fix`, `investigate`, `stats`, `logs`, `actions`, `audit`, `config`, `circuit`, `watch`, `notify`, `tui`, `repl`, `setup`. [4]\",\r\r\n      \"status\": \"GROUNDED\",\r\r\n      \"query_id\": \"q-6ad52b07fded\",\r\r\n      \"tokens\": 261,\r\r\n      \"created_at\": 1793967625.763424,\r\r\n      \"citations\": [\r\r\n        {\r\r\n          \"document\": \"docs/lear_backend/README.md\",\r\r\n          \"heading\": \"Lear backend — engineering documentation > How to read these pages\"\r\r\n        },\r\r\n        {\r\r\n          \"document\": \"docs/lear_backend/README.md\",\r\r\n          \"heading\": \"Lear backend — engineering documentation > What Lear is\"\r\r\n        },\r\r\n        {\r\r\n          \"document\": \"docs/lear_backend/reference/cli.md\",\r\r\n          \"heading\": \"Lear backend — CLI reference (`prash`)\"\r\r\n        }\r\r\n      ]\r\r\n    },\r\r\n    {\r\r\n      \"message_id\": 33,\r\r\n      \"session_id\": \"rec-s07-20261106T1219Z\",\r\r\n      \"user_id\": \"rec-u07\",\r\r\n      \"role\": \"user\",\r\r\n      \"content\": \"Does `prash run --dry-run` execute the action?\",\r\r\n      \"status\": null,\r\r\n      \"query_id\": null,\r\r\n      \"tokens\": 12,\r\r\n      \"created_at\": 1793967625.9595873,\r\r\n      \"citations\": []\r\r\n    },\r\r\n    {\r\r\n      \"message_id\": 34,\r\r\n      \"session_id\": \"rec-s07-20261106T1219Z\",\r\r\n      \"user_id\": \"rec-u07\",\r\r\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\r\n      \"content\": \"Evidence: `prash/cli.py:L1252`, `prash/cli.py:L273`. - [implemented] `--dry-run` plans without touching infrastructure, `--grant` pre-grants a single action, and `--noninteractive` never prompts (a missing secret then returns NEEDS_INPUT). [4]\",\r\r\n      \"status\": \"GROUNDED\",\r\r\n      \"query_id\": \"q-0a39f90321ee\",\r\r\n      \"tokens\": 61,\r\r\n      \"created_at\": 1793967625.961405,\r\r\n      \"citations\": [\r\r\n        {\r\r\n          \"document\": \"docs/lear_backend/api_reference.md\",\r\r\n          \"heading\": \"API reference > The `prash` CLI\"\r\r\n        }\r\r\n      ]\r\r\n    },\r\r\n    {\r\r\n      \"message_id\": 35,\r\r\n      \"session_id\": \"rec-s07-20261106T1219Z\",\r\r\n      \"user_id\": \"rec-u07\",\r\r\n      \"role\": \"user\",\r\r\n      \"content\": \"What happens when the permission engine returns PROMPT but `prash run` was started with --noninteractive?\",\r\r\n      \"status\": null,\r\r\n      \"query_id\": null,\r\r\n      \"tokens\": 27,\r\r\n      \"created_at\": 1793967626.163668,\r\r\n      \"citations\": []\r\r\n    },\r\r\n    {\r\r\n      \"message_id\": 36,\r\r\n      \"session_id\": \"rec-s07-20261106T1219Z\",\r\r\n      \"user_id\": \"rec-u07\",\r\r\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\r\n      \"content\": \"Evidence: `prash/server.py:L2641-L2700`. - [implemented] For the duration of that call the handler swaps `cli.CliAsk` for an ask object that always answers yes, so prompts raised by the permission engine are approved automatically. [1] Evidence: `prash/cli.py:L1254`, `prash/cli.py:L277`. - [implemented] A dry run consults the permission engine but never calls `execute`; a refusal is reported as refused instead of showing a plan. [3]\",\r\r\n      \"status\": \"GROUNDED\",\r\r\n      \"query_id\": \"q-dea61f02dcba\",\r\r\n      \"tokens\": 109,\r\r\n      \"created_at\": 1793967626.1651292,\r\r\n      \"citations\": [\r\r\n        {\r\r\n          \"document\": \"docs/lear_backend/api_reference.md\",\r\r\n          \"heading\": \"API reference > The desktop HTTP/WebSocket API > Selected endpoints\"\r\r\n        },\r\r\n        {\r\r\n          \"document\": \"docs/lear_backend/authentication_authorization.md\",\r\r\n          \"heading\": \"Authentication and authorization > Dry runs\"\r\r\n        }\r\r\n      ]\r\r\n    },\r\r\n    {\r\r\n      \"message_id\": 37,\r\r\n      \"session_id\": \"rec-s07-20261106T1219Z\",\r\r\n      \"user_id\": \"rec-u07\",\r\r\n      \"role\": \"u"]
[2.095602, "o", "ser\",\r\r\n      \"content\": \"Which subcommands does the prash CLI provide?\",\r\r\n      \"status\": null,\r\r\n      \"query_id\": null,\r\r\n      \"tokens\": 12,\r\r\n      \"created_at\": 1793967626.375882,\r\r\n      \"citations\": []\r\r\n    },\r\r\n    {\r\r\n      \"message_id\": 38,\r\r\n      \"session_id\": \"rec-s07-20261106T1219Z\",\r\r\n      \"user_id\": \"rec-u07\",\r\r\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\r\n      \"content\": \"Evidence: `prash/server.py:L704-L722`. - [implemented] `POST /api/chat/execute` (`execute_chat_action`) turns a JSON `command` list (or an action id) into CLI arguments, prefixing `run` when the first word is not a known subcommand, and re-enters `cli.build_parser()` in the same process. [1] Reversible: True. - Class: `TerraformInitAction` at `prash/actions/terraform_init.py:L16-L78`; spec at `prash/actions/terraform_init.py:L17-L23`. - Registered in the CLI dispatcher: yes. - Contract methods defined in the class: execute, plan, verify. - Summary (from the spec): Run terraform init to download modules and providers. - Capabilities: `('init',)`. [4]\",\r\r\n      \"status\": \"GROUNDED\",\r\r\n      \"query_id\": \"q-1ccecd66e3b7\",\r\r\n      \"tokens\": 165,\r\r\n      \"created_at\": 1793967626.3777385,\r\r\n      \"citations\": [\r\r\n        {\r\r\n          \"document\": \"docs/lear_backend/api_reference.md\",\r\r\n          \"heading\": \"API reference > The desktop HTTP/WebSocket API > Selected endpoints\"\r\r\n        },\r\r\n        {\r\r\n          \"document\": \"docs/lear_backend/reference/actions.md\",\r\r\n          \"heading\": \"Lear backend — action catalogue > Safe-tier actions > terraform-init\"\r\r\n        }\r\r\n      ]\r\r\n    },\r\r\n    {\r\r\n      \"message_id\": 39,\r\r\n      \"session_id\": \"rec-s07-20261106T1219Z\",\r\r\n      \"user_id\": \"rec-u07\",\r\r\n      \"role\": \"user\",\r\r\n      \"content\": \"Which permission mode does `prash run` use when --mode is not given?\",\r\r\n      \"status\": null,\r\r\n      \"query_id\": null,\r\r\n      \"tokens\": 17,\r\r\n      \"created_at\": 1793967626.5766675,\r\r\n      \"citations\": []\r\r\n    },\r\r\n    {\r\r\n      \"message_id\": 40,\r\r\n      \"session_id\": \"rec-s07-20261106T1219Z\","]
[2.095761, "o", "\r\r\n      \"user_id\": \"rec-u07\",\r\r\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\r\n      \"content\": \"Evidence: `prash/cli.py:L348-L350`. - 2. [implemented] Resolve the permission mode from `--mode`, else `PRASH_PERMISSION_MODE`, else `ask`, and build a dispatcher for it. [1] Common options on the acting subcommands: - [implemented] `--mode` selects the permission mode (read-only, ask, auto-safe, environment-scoped, bypass); when omitted, `run` and `fix` read `PRASH_PERMISSION_MODE` from the credentials file and fall back to `ask`. [3]\",\r\r\n      \"status\": \"GROUNDED\",\r\r\n      \"query_id\": \"q-c6e759b1f1fd\",\r\r\n      \"tokens\": 110,\r\r\n      \"created_at\": 1793967626.5785549,\r\r\n      \"citations\": [\r\r\n        {\r\r\n          \"document\": \"docs/lear_backend/services_and_workflows.md\",\r\r\n          \"heading\": \"Services and workflows > `prash run`: one action through the pipeline\"\r\r\n        },\r\r\n        {\r\r\n          \"document\": \"docs/lear_backend/api_reference.md\",\r\r\n          \"heading\": \"API reference > The `prash` CLI\"\r\r\n        }\r\r\n      ]\r\r\n    },\r\r\n    {\r\r\n      \"message_id\": 41,\r\r\n      \"session_id\": \"rec-s07-20261106T1219Z\",\r\r\n      \"user_id\": \"rec-u07\",\r\r\n      \"role\": \"user\",\r\r\n      \"content\": \"Going back to the state file from my second question: what happens if that file is corrupted?\",\r\r\n      \"status\": null,\r\r\n      \"query_id\": null,\r\r\n      \"tokens\": 24,\r\r\n      \"created_at\": 1793967626.785702,\r\r\n      \"citations\": []\r\r\n    },\r\r\n    {\r\r\n      \"message_id\": 42,\r\r\n      \"session_id\": \"rec-s07-20261106T1219Z\",\r\r\n      \"user_id\": \"rec-u07\",\r\r\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\r\n      \"content\": \"Evidence: `prash/cli.py:L348-L350`. - 2. [implemented] Resolve the permission mode from `--mode`, else `PRASH_PERMISSION_MODE`, else `ask`, and build a dispatcher for it. [3] Common options on the acting subcommands: - [implemented] `--mode` selects the permission mode (read-only, ask, auto-safe, environment-scoped, bypass); when omitted, `run` and `fix` read `PRASH_PERMISSION_MODE` from the credentials file and fall back to `ask`. [1]\",\r\r\n      \"status\": \"GROUNDED\",\r\r\n      \"query_id\": \"q-a"]
